-- title:
--   Saturation of the eigen-ideal submodule in the ordinary corner
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, $p$ a prime with $p \neq 2$ lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, and $\bar\rho$ a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, factoring through a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ and absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to the algebraic closure of the residue field). Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p \in S$, $M$ a nonzero natural number all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$ with $p^2 \nmid M$, and $S_{\min} \subseteq S$ a subset containing $p$ whose primes $q \neq p$ are exactly those at which $\bar\rho$ is ramified; the arithmetic hypotheses on the level — divisibility conditions relating $M$ to $S_{\min}$ (primes of $S_{\min}$ other than $p$ divide $M$; primes $q \neq p$ dividing $M$ but outside $S_{\min}$ divide $M$ at least twice and never three times), unipotence of inertia at the primes $q \in S_{\min}$, $q \neq p$, and ordinarity of $\bar\rho$ at $p$ when $p \mid M$ — are summarised here. Let $r$ be a prime with $r \notin S$, $r \nmid M$, $p \nmid r-1$, and such that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $r$ and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $r$ for $P$ one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2 \neq (r+1)^2$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$M$ Hecke algebra, anemic outside $S$, to the residue field, such that the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho$ at Frobenius at any prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid M$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$, and let $\pi_T$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map from the localised Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeLocal M S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) to $\mathcal{O}$. Put $L = Mr$ and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$ be the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/r)^\times$. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, module-finite over $\mathcal{O}$, acting $\mathcal{O}$-compatibly on $H^1 = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L)^{\mathrm{ab}}, \mathcal{O})$, let $\mathrm{Sp}$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb{T}$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_j$ together with the maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_j$, every maximal ideal occurring, with $e_j \in \mathfrak{m}_k$ exactly when $j \neq k$) and $i$ an index, the corner $e_i H^1$ being finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$. Further data are families $t$ and $c$ indexed by the Hecke generators [`CohCarrier.Gen L S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) with values in $\mathbb{T}$ and in $\mathcal{O}$: the action of $\mathbb{T}$ on $H^1$ lands in the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the operators [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) at the guarded generators (those $g$ for which $g = U_q$ forces $q \mid M$), $t(g)$ acts as the corresponding operator for guarded $g$, $t(g) - c(g) \in \mathfrak{m}_i$, any $v \in H^1$ annihilated modulo every power of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$ by a power of each $t(g)-c(g)$ lies in the corner, the residue of $c(T_\ell)$ equals $\theta(T_\ell)$, $c(U_q)$ is in the maximal ideal for $q \mid M$, $q \neq p$, $q^2 \mid M$, $c(U_p)$ is a unit when $p \mid M$, and $c(\langle d\rangle) \equiv 1$. Finally the corner is nonzero, the corner ring $e_i \mathbb{T} e_i$ acts faithfully on it, and $e$ is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra isomorphism from the corner ring onto [`CuspForm.heckeLocal M S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) carrying the image of $T_\ell$ to the operator `heckeT` for primes $\ell \notin S$ not dividing $M$ or $L$. The conclusion: writing $\mathfrak{p}$ for the kernel of $\pi_T \circ e$ as an ideal of the corner ring, for every nonzero $a \in \mathcal{O}$ and every $m$ in the corner, $a \cdot m \in \mathfrak{p} \cdot (e_i H^1)$ implies $m \in \mathfrak{p} \cdot (e_i H^1)$.
--
--   This is the saturation (torsion-freeness of the quotient) of the submodule cut out by the eigen-ideal of an $\mathcal{O}$-valued point of the local Hecke algebra inside the ordinary corner of $H^1$ at the auxiliary level $Mr$. It feeds the construction of the unit-root refinement package for the corner data, where a torsion-free quotient is needed to compare congruence modules with the cotangent space of the point.
